<title>ESTONIA: SILMET STATE STAKE TO BE PUT IN PUBLIC OFFER.</title>
<headline>SILMET STATE STAKE TO BE PUT IN PUBLIC OFFER.</headline>
<dateline>TALLINN 1997-05-20</dateline>
<text>
<p>Estonian economics minister Jaak Leimann said on Tuesday that the state plans to sell its 35 percent stake in the chemical processing plant Silmet through a public offer.</p>
<p>Silmet, one of Estonia's largest companies, was privatized at the end of last year and bought by Ephag, which is a part of the Magnum Group. </p>
<p>Leimann also told a news conference that stakes in furniture company Tarmeko, sewing company Lembitu, Hotel Olumpia, Estonian Metal Export Company and Eesti Gaas (Estonian Gas) will be sold through a public offer.</p>
<p>-- Eva Palu, Tallinn Newsroom, +372 630 8400, reuters@reuters.ee</p>
</text>
